First we consider the vectors going to the corners labelled $A,B,C,D$. Thus, the vectors are $(0,0)$, $\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1\\ 1 \end{pmatrix}$, $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \\ - 1 \end{pmatrix}$, $\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}$, $\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$, and $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}$. Then the diagonals are $\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}$, $\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}$. So we need to compute $\cos \theta=\frac{\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}\cdot \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}}{\left | \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} \right |\left | \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 3 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix} \right |}$. Here $\theta$ is the angle between these two vectors.
